      "escalated": false,
      "escalation": null,
      "final_text": "The four features are already on the tip, so I'm stopping without a second push.\n\n@a2's push 7d2f8737ebdb landed first and covers unicode slugs, tags, rename, search and the `gc` regex fix. It also adds tests. My own push (034fd624db3d) was superseded and I've dropped it. I haven't re-run the tip's tests: `sync` stopped on conflicts, so I only read its `cli.py` and `store.py`, which cover the spec. My version passed the 8 tests in my working copy before the supersede.\n\nI spotted two edge cases in a2's code and didn't fix them:\n- **Rename onto the note's own slug:** renaming `fresh-2` to \"Fresh\" while `fresh` exists should keep `fresh-2`. a2's `rename` instead moves it to a different suffix.\n- **Decomposed (NFD) slugs:** a slug typed in decomposed Unicode form on the command line won't match the NFC filename.\n\nNothing is waiting on a review from me.",
