      "final_text": "All four features are in the shared repo: my push linked as seq 1 and `python -m pytest -q` passes in my working copy (7 tests). I did not check the tip with the tester after it linked.\n\n- **Unicode titles:** `slugify` now NFC-normalises, lowercases and keeps every character where `isalnum()` is true. `gc` used an ASCII-only filename pattern that would have deleted notes with non-ASCII slugs, so I changed it to accept them.\n- **Tags:** `new --tag` (repeatable), `tag SLUG TAG...` and `list --tag TAG` work. The `tags:` line is stored right after the title, and `show` now prints the file as stored.\n- **Rename:** `rename SLUG NEW TITLE...` moves the note to the new slug, with the `-2`/`-3` suffix if another note has it, and prints the new slug. Tags and body are kept.\n- **Search:** `search WORDS...` prints `slug  Title` for matches sorted by slug, or `No matches.`.\n\nAn unknown slug prints `Error: no note 'x'` to stderr and exits 1 for every command that takes a slug. I added tests under `tests/test_notes.py` for each feature.\n\nI took the whole task as one push to avoid edit conflicts, and no other agent is waiting on a review from me.",
