      "final_text": "I made no changes myself. @a2 held a claim on every file and landed all four features, so I stayed out of their way.\n\nI synced to their change and checked it. `python -m pytest -q` passes (7 tests). I also ran the commands by hand in a throwaway directory:\n- `new Caf\u00e9 au lait --tag Home --tag home` creates `caf\u00e9-au-lait` with one `home` tag.\n- `tag` prints `Tagged caf\u00e9-au-lait: home, errand`.\n- `rename` to `\u6771\u4eac \u30e1\u30e2` returns `\u6771\u4eac-\u30e1\u30e2`.\n- `search \u30e1\u30e2` prints `\u6771\u4eac-\u30e1\u30e2  \u6771\u4eac \u30e1\u30e2`.\n- `show` on the renamed note prints the stored file, with the `tags:` line right after the title.\n- `show x` prints `Error: no note 'x'` and exits 1.\n\nI didn't hand-check the other subcommands or the `-2`/`-3` collision suffix on rename. Nobody is waiting on a review from me.",
